/-!
# The cycle of the zero scheme of a regular section, component by component

In Situation 0EDT let `X/B` be good, let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, let `s ∈ Γ(X, ℒ)` be
a regular section and assume `dim_δ(X) ≤ k + 1`. Write `[X]_{k+1} = ∑ n_i [X_i]` over the
irreducible components `X_i` of δ-dimension `k + 1`. **Stacks 0EQL** asserts

`[Z(s)]_k = ∑ n_i [Z(s|_{X_i})]_k`

as `k`-cycles on `X`. This file proves it, with nothing carried.

The proof is local at the generic point `ξ` of an integral closed subspace `T` of δ-dimension `k`.
On an affine étale chart `W` of `X` through `ξ` on which `ℒ` is free with coordinate `l₀`, let
`A = 𝒪_{W, w}` and let `f` be the germ of `l₀(s)`. Every multiplicity in the identity is a colength
in `A`:

* the multiplicity of `T` in `Z(s)` is the colength of `(f)`, the defining ideal of `Z(s)` on `W`
  being generated by `l₀(s)` (Stacks 0846);
* for an integral closed subspace `V`, the multiplicity of `T` in `Z(s|_V)` is the colength of
  `(f) + I_V`, where `I_V` is the ideal of `V` in `A`: on the chart `W ×_X V` of `V` the generator
  of `ℒ` restricts to a generator of `ℒ|_V` and the coordinate of `s|_V` is the restriction of
  that of `s`;
* the multiplicity `n_V` is the length of `A` localized at any minimal prime lying over the
  generic point of `V`.

The minimal primes of `A` lie over the generic points of the components of δ-dimension `k + 1`
through `ξ`, since `A` has dimension one; those over a given component `V` are exactly the minimal
primes of the radical ideal `I_V`. So the identity is the colength formula of Stacks 02QG grouped
along this partition,
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_length_quotient_span_eq_finsum_length_quotient_sup`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBranchComponent`: the component of δ-dimension `k + 1` that a
  minimal prime of a chart local ring lies over.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartComponentIdeal`: the ideal of an integral closed subspace in a
  local ring of an affine chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IntegralClosedSubspace.baseChangeChartSection`: the restriction of a
  section of `ℒ` over a chart to the base-changed chart of an integral closed subspace.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_length_quotient` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentZeroCycleCoeff_eq_length_quotient`: the two sides of the
  identity at `T`, as colengths in `A`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.minimalPrimes_chartComponentIdeal`: the minimal primes of `I_V` are the
  minimal primes of `A` over `V`.
* `cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_componentZeroCycleSumCoeff_of_isRegularSection`:
  `[Z(s)]_k = ∑ n_i [Z(s_i)]_k` as `k`-cycles on `X`.

## Implementation notes

Both sides are coefficient families on the integral closed subspaces of `X`, which is the form in
which the cycle `[Y]_k` of a closed subspace, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace`,
and the sum `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentZeroCycleSumCoeff` are stated. The latter is the
right-hand side of Stacks 0EQL as the library already states it, with `n_i` the coefficient of
`X_i` in `[X]_{k+1} = [𝒪_X]_{k+1}` and `s|_{X_i}` the inverse image along `X_i → X`.

The chart computations on `W ×_X V` are stated over an arbitrary base `(B, S)` rather than over
the base of Situation 0EDT: they are statements about one algebraic space and one closed
subspace, and nothing of the dimension theory enters them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EQL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EQL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EPI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EPI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02QG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0845](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0845)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0846](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0846)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EE1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EE1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EE9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EE9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EED](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EED)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

open TopologicalSpace.IrreducibleCloseds (closureSingleton)

universe u

namespace TopologicalSpace

/-- **A point at which a dimension function is one below its maximum has codimension at most
one.** If `d ≤ k + 1` everywhere and `d z = k`, then a chain `{z}‾ ⊊ Z₁ ⊊ Z₂` of irreducible
closed sets would give generic points `ζ₂ ⤳ ζ₁ ⤳ z`, all distinct, so `d ζ₂ ≥ k + 2`. -/
theorem codimension_closureSingleton_le_one {A : Type*} [TopologicalSpace A] [QuasiSober A]
    (d : DimensionFunction A) {k : ℤ} (hd : ∀ y, d y ≤ k + 1) (z : A) (hz : d z = k) :
    codimension (closureSingleton z) ≤ 1 := by
  rw [codimension_eq_coheight]
  refine Order.coheight_le fun p hp => ?_
  by_contra hlt
  push Not at hlt
  have h2 : 2 ≤ p.length := by
    have : (1 : ℕ∞) < p.length := hlt
    exact_mod_cast Order.add_one_le_of_lt this
  -- the generic points of the first two members after the head
  have hgen : ∀ Z : IrreducibleCloseds A, ∃ ζ : A, IsGenericPoint ζ (Z : Set A) := fun Z =>
    QuasiSober.sober Z.isIrreducible Z.isClosed
  obtain ⟨ζ₁, hζ₁⟩ := hgen (p ⟨1, by omega⟩)
  obtain ⟨ζ₂, hζ₂⟩ := hgen (p ⟨2, by omega⟩)
  have h01 : p 0 < p ⟨1, by omega⟩ := p.strictMono (Fin.mk_lt_mk.mpr (by norm_num))
  have h12 : p ⟨1, by omega⟩ < p ⟨2, by omega⟩ := p.strictMono (Fin.mk_lt_mk.mpr (by norm_num))
  have hp0 : p 0 = closureSingleton z := hp
  -- strict specializations between the generic points
  have hspec : ∀ {Z Z' : IrreducibleCloseds A} {ζ ζ' : A}, IsGenericPoint ζ (Z : Set A) →
      IsGenericPoint ζ' (Z' : Set A) → Z < Z' → ζ' ⤳ ζ ∧ ζ' ≠ ζ := by
    intro Z Z' ζ ζ' hζ hζ' hZZ'
    refine ⟨hζ'.specializes (hZZ'.le (hζ.mem)), fun h => ?_⟩
    subst h
    exact hZZ'.ne (IrreducibleCloseds.ext (hζ.symm.trans hζ'))
  have hz0 : IsGenericPoint z ((p 0 : IrreducibleCloseds A) : Set A) := by
    rw [hp0]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨hs1, hn1⟩ := hspec hz0 hζ₁ h01
  obtain ⟨hs2, hn2⟩ := hspec hζ₁ hζ₂ h12
  have hd1 := d.strictAnti_specializes hs1 hn1
  have hd2 := d.strictAnti_specializes hs2 hn2
  have := hd ζ₂
  omega

end TopologicalSpace

namespace Ideal

/-- In a local ring of dimension at most one, a prime ideal other than the maximal ideal is a
minimal prime: a strictly smaller prime would give a chain of length two. -/
theorem mem_minimalPrimes_of_ne_maximalIdeal {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (hdim : ringKrullDim A ≤ 1) {q : Ideal A} [hq : q.IsPrime]
    (hne : q ≠ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) : q ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  refine ⟨⟨hq, bot_le⟩, fun p hp hpq => ?_⟩
  by_contra hqp
  have hlt1 : (⟨p, hp.1⟩ : PrimeSpectrum A) < ⟨q, hq⟩ :=
    lt_of_le_of_ne hpq fun h => hqp (by rw [show p = q from congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal h])
  have hlt2 : (⟨q, hq⟩ : PrimeSpectrum A) < IsLocalRing.closedPoint A :=
    lt_of_le_of_ne (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hq.ne_top) fun h =>
      hne (congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal h)
  let l₁ : LTSeries (PrimeSpectrum A) :=
    (RelSeries.singleton _ (⟨p, hp.1⟩ : PrimeSpectrum A)).snoc ⟨q, hq⟩ (by simpa using hlt1)
  let l : LTSeries (PrimeSpectrum A) :=
    l₁.snoc (IsLocalRing.closedPoint A) (by simpa [l₁] using hlt2)
  have hlen := Order.LTSeries.length_le_krullDim l
  have h2 : (l.length : WithBot ℕ∞) = ((2 : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by simp [l, l₁]
  rw [h2] at hlen
  have h3 : ((2 : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ((1 : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := hlen.trans hdim
  exact absurd (WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp h3) (by norm_num)

/-- A local ring of dimension at most one containing a nonzerodivisor in its maximal ideal has
dimension exactly one. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_eq_one_of_mem_maximalIdeal {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (h1 : ringKrullDim A ≤ 1) {f : A} (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors A)
    (hm : f ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) : ringKrullDim A = 1 := by
  refine le_antisymm h1 ?_
  have hproper : Ideal.span {f} ≠ ⊤ :=
    ne_top_of_le_ne_top (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).ne_top
      (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hm))
  have : Nontrivial (A ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hproper
  exact (show (1 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (A ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) + 1 by
    simpa only [zero_add, add_comm] using add_le_add_right
      (ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial (R := A ⧸ Ideal.span {f})) 1).trans
    (ringKrullDim_quotient_succ_le_of_nonZeroDivisor hf)

/-- A ring isomorphism preserves the length of a ring over itself. -/
theorem length_self_eq_of_ringEquiv {R T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing T] (e : R ≃+* T) :
    Module.length R R = Module.length T T := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Module.length_self_eq_length_quotient_ker e.toRingHom e.surjective]
  have hker : RingHom.ker e.toRingHom = ⊥ := (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp e.injective
  rw [hker]
  exact (Submodule.quotEquivOfEqBot (⊥ : Ideal R) rfl).length_eq.symm

/-- The quotient of a ring by the unit ideal has length zero. -/
private theorem length_quotient_top_eq_zero {R : Type*} [CommRing R] :
    Module.length R (R ⧸ (⊤ : Ideal R)) = 0 :=
  haveI : Subsingleton (R ⧸ (⊤ : Ideal R)) := Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.mpr rfl
  Module.length_eq_zero

end Ideal

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology
attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable

variable (D : BaseSpaceDimensionSituation.{u})
    {X : (BigFppfOver D.site D.base D.base_mem)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (sX : X ⟶ D.space)
    (hX : D.IsGood sX)

/-- The generic point of an integral closed subspace `T` lies outside a closed subspace `Z`
unless `T ⊆ Z`. -/
private theorem notMem_subspacePointSet_of_ambientGenericPoint_eq
    (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (T : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (Z : Subfunctor X)
    (hZ : IsClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem Z)
    (hTZ : ¬ subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X T.subspace ⊆
      subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X Z)
    {p : points D.site D.base D.base_mem X}
    (hp : p = T.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem) :
    p ∉ subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X Z := by
  intro h
  refine hTZ ?_
  rw [hp] at h
  rw [← (T.isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem hY).def]
  exact (isClosed_subspacePointSet_of_isClosedSubspace D hY Z hZ).closure_subset_iff.2
    (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 h)

/-! ### The local ring of a chart at a point of δ-dimension `k` -/

section LocalRing

variable {k : ℤ}
    (hdim : deltaDimensionClosed D sX hX Set.univ isClosed_univ ≤ ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt))

include hdim in
/-- On a good space of δ-dimension at most `k + 1`, `δ_{X/B} ≤ k + 1` at every point. -/
theorem deltaValue_le_of_deltaDimensionClosed_le (x : points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) :
    D.deltaValue sX x ≤ k + 1 :=
  (deltaDimensionClosed_le_coe_iff D sX hX Set.univ isClosed_univ (k + 1)).mp hdim x
    (Set.mem_univ x)

include hdim in
/-- **The local ring of an étale chart at a point over a point of δ-dimension `k` has dimension at
most one**, on a good space of δ-dimension at most `k + 1`: its dimension is the codimension of
the closure of the image point (Stacks 04NA, 0ED1), which is at most one by
`TopologicalSpace.codimension_closureSingleton_le_one`. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_stalk_chartScheme_le_one (W : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (w : chartScheme W)
    (hw : D.deltaValue sX (chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w) = k) :
    ringKrullDim ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) ≤ 1 := by
  have : QuasiSober (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) := quasiSober_points_of_isGood D sX hX
  rw [ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight w,
    coheight_eq_codimension_chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) W w]
  have h := codimension_closureSingleton_le_one (deltaDimensionFunction D sX hX)
    (k := k) (fun y => by
      rw [deltaDimensionFunction_apply]
      exact deltaValue_le_of_deltaDimensionClosed_le D sX hX hdim y)
    (chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w)
    (by rw [deltaDimensionFunction_apply]; exact hw)
  exact_mod_cast h

end LocalRing

/-! ### The ideal of a closed subspace in a local ring of an affine chart -/

section ClosedSubspaceIdeal

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
    {Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y)
    (Z : Subfunctor Y) (hZ : IsClosedSubspace B S hS Z) (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y)
    [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]

/-- **On an affine chart, the stalk of the ideal sheaf of the base change of a closed subspace is
the ideal generated by its defining ideal.** -/
theorem stalk_ker_snd_eq_map_germ_definingIdealAt (a : chartScheme W) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (Scheme.Hom.ker ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hZ.2.rep.snd W.obj.hom))) a =
      Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
        (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ (op W)) := by
  let : AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hZ.2.rep.snd W.obj.hom)) :=
    hZ.2.property_snd W.obj.hom
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ
      (Scheme.Hom.ker ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hZ.2.rep.snd W.obj.hom))) a
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top (chartScheme W)⟩ trivial,
    AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_apply
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (hZ.2.rep.snd W.obj.hom))
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top (chartScheme W)⟩,
    definingIdealAt_eq_ker B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ W]
  rfl

/-- **On an affine chart, the ideal generated in a local ring by the defining ideal of a closed
subspace is the unit ideal at a point off the subspace**: some element of the defining ideal does
not vanish there. -/
theorem map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top (a : chartScheme W)
    (ha : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS Y W a ∉ subspacePointSet B S hS Y Z) :
    Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
        (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ (op W)) = ⊤ := by
  have : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W.obj.left) := ‹IsAffine (chartScheme W)›
  have hrange := range_rep_snd_eq_zeroLocus_definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ W
  have hnot : a ∉ ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W.1.left).zeroLocus
      {k : Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W.1.left, ⊤) |
        k ∈ definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ (op W)} := by
    rw [← hrange]
    rintro ⟨b, hb⟩
    refine ha ?_
    rw [← hb]
    have h := chartSchemeToPoints_map_chartDiagram B S hS
      (⟨(smallBaseChange B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY Z hZ) hZ.2.rep).obj W, W,
        hZ.2.rep.snd W.obj.hom, (hZ.2.rep.isPullback W.obj.hom).w⟩ :
          ChartDiagram B S hS Z.toFunctor Y (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY Z hZ).hom) b
    exact h ▸ ⟨_, rfl⟩
  rw [Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff] at hnot
  push Not at hnot
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hga⟩ := hnot
  exact Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hg)
    ((Scheme.mem_basicOpen _ g a trivial).1 hga)

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top` for a bundled closed subspace. -/
theorem map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top' (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS Y) (a : chartScheme W)
    (ha : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS Y W a ∉ subspacePointSet B S hS Y Z.1) :
    Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
        (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ Z (op W)) = ⊤ :=
  map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top hY Z.1 Z.2 W a ha

/-- **On an affine chart where `ℒ` is free, the ideal of the zero scheme of `s` in a local ring of
the chart is generated by the germ of the coordinate of `s`.** -/
theorem map_germ_definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_eq_span (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y hY)
    (hinv : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩).property L)
    (s : L.sections) (t : L.val.obj (op W))
    (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing B S hS Y hY W) (L.val.obj (op W))) (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • t = x)
    (a : chartScheme W) :
    Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
        (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ (zeroScheme B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ L s) (op W)) =
      Ideal.span {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} := by
  have hdef := definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_eq_span_generator_of_isInvertible B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ L
    hinv s W ‹_› t l₀ hb
  rw [hdef]
  exact (Ideal.map_span _ _).trans (congrArg _ Set.image_singleton)

end ClosedSubspaceIdeal

/-! ### Lengths at geometric points read on a chart -/

section ChartLengths

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **The length of the structure sheaf at a geometric point is the length of the local ring of
any étale chart at a point over it** (Stacks 0EE1). -/
theorem geometricLength_unit_eq_length_stalk (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (y : GeometricPoint B S hS Y.1) (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) (p : chartScheme W)
    (hp : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS Y.1 W p = y.image) :
    geometricLength B S hS Y y (SheafOfModules.unit _) =
      Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk p) ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk p) := by
  obtain ⟨V, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_smallEtaleNeighborhood_chart_eq B S hS Y y W p hp
  exact geometricLength_unit_eq_length_chartLocalRing B S hS Y y V

/-- **The multiplicity of a closed subspace at a geometric point is a colength on any affine
étale chart of the ambient space**, at any point of the chart over the image of the geometric
point. -/
theorem geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints
    {Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y)
    (Z : Subfunctor Y) (hZ : IsClosedSubspace B S hS Z) (z : GeometricPoint B S hS Z.toFunctor)
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y) [IsAffine (chartScheme W)] (a : chartScheme W)
    (ha : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS Y W a = pointsMap B S hS Z.toFunctor Z.ι z.image) :
    geometricLength B S hS ⟨Z.toFunctor, hZ.1⟩ z (SheafOfModules.unit _) =
      Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk a)
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk a ⧸
          Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
            (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ ⟨Z, hZ⟩ (op W))) := by
  obtain ⟨A, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_smallEtaleNeighborhood_chart_eq B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩
    (geometricPointMap (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY Z hZ).hom z) W a
    (ha.trans (geometricPointMap_image _ z).symm)
  exact geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt B S hS hY Z hZ z A
    ‹_› _ (chartPoint_baseChange B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY Z hZ) hZ.2.rep z A)

/-- `geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints` for a bundled
closed subspace. -/
theorem geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints'
    {Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y)
    (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS Y) (z : GeometricPoint B S hS Z.1.toFunctor)
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y) [IsAffine (chartScheme W)] (a : chartScheme W)
    (ha : chartSchemeToPoints B S hS Y W a = pointsMap B S hS Z.1.toFunctor Z.1.ι z.image) :
    geometricLength B S hS ⟨Z.1.toFunctor, Z.2.1⟩ z (SheafOfModules.unit _) =
      Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk a)
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk a ⧸
          Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ a trivial).hom
            (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩ Z (op W))) :=
  geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints hY Z.1 Z.2 z W a ha

/-- **For a surjective ring map `φ : A → B` and an element `f ∈ A`, the colength of `φ(f)` in `B`
is the colength of `(f) + ker φ` in `A`.** -/
theorem length_quotient_span_map_eq_length_quotient_sup_ker {A B : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] (φ : A →+* B) (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (f : A) :
    Module.length B (B ⧸ Ideal.span {φ f}) =
      Module.length A (A ⧸ (Ideal.span {f} ⊔ RingHom.ker φ)) := by
  let ψ : A →+* B ⧸ Ideal.span {φ f} := (Ideal.Quotient.mk _).comp φ
  have hψ : Function.Surjective ψ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.comp hφ
  have hker : RingHom.ker ψ = Ideal.span {f} ⊔ RingHom.ker φ := by
    rw [show ψ = (Ideal.Quotient.mk _).comp φ from rfl, ← RingHom.comap_ker, Ideal.mk_ker,
      show Ideal.span {φ f} = Ideal.map φ (Ideal.span {f}) by
        rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton],
      Ideal.comap_map_of_surjective' φ hφ]
  rw [← hker, ← Module.length_self_eq_length_quotient_ker ψ hψ]
  exact Module.length_eq_of_surjective (R := B ⧸ Ideal.span {φ f}) (S := B)
    (M := B ⧸ Ideal.span {φ f}) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- **For a closed immersion `φ : T → W`, the colength in `𝒪_{T, y}` of the pullback of a global
function `g` on `W` is the colength in `𝒪_{W, φ y}` of `g` together with the kernel of the stalk
map.** -/
theorem length_quotient_span_germ_appTop {T W : Scheme.{u}} (φ : T ⟶ W)
    [_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion φ] (g : Γ(W, ⊤)) (y : T) :
    Module.length (T.presheaf.stalk y)
        (T.presheaf.stalk y ⧸ Ideal.span {(T.presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom (φ.appTop.hom g)}) =
      Module.length (W.presheaf.stalk (φ y))
        (W.presheaf.stalk (φ y) ⧸
          (Ideal.span {(W.presheaf.germ ⊤ (φ y) trivial).hom g} ⊔
            RingHom.ker (φ.stalkMap y).hom)) := by
  have hgerm : (T.presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom (φ.appTop.hom g) =
      (φ.stalkMap y).hom ((W.presheaf.germ ⊤ (φ y) trivial).hom g) :=
    (Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply φ ⊤ y trivial g).symm
  rw [hgerm]
  exact length_quotient_span_map_eq_length_quotient_sup_ker _ (φ.stalkMap_surjective y) _

end ChartLengths

/-! ### The restriction of a section to an integral closed subspace, read on a chart -/

section RestrictedSection

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
    {Y : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hY : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Y)
    (V : IntegralClosedSubspace B S hS Y) (L : Modules.{u, u} B S hS Y hY)
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS Y)

/-- **The square `(W', W)` over the closed immersion `V → Y`** for a chart `W'` of `V` over the
base change `W ×_Y V`. -/
abbrev IntegralClosedSubspace.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram
    {W' : SmallEtale B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor} (k : W' ⟶ V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) :
    ChartDiagram B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor Y
      (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace).hom where
  U := W'
  V := W
  g := (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).map k ≫
    (V.baseChangeChartDiagram B S hS hY W).g
  comm := by
    change W'.obj.hom ≫ (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace).hom =
      yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).map k ≫
        (V.baseChangeChartDiagram B S hS hY W).g) ≫ W.obj.hom
    refine (congrArg (· ≫ (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace).hom)
      (CostructuredArrow.w k.hom).symm).trans ?_
    refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ?_
    refine (congrArg (yoneda.map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).map k) ≫ ·)
      (V.baseChangeChartDiagram B S hS hY W).comm).trans ?_
    refine (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans ?_
    exact congrArg (· ≫ W.obj.hom) (yoneda.map_comp _ _).symm

/-- **The restriction of a section `t` of `ℒ` over `W` to `ℒ|_V`** over a chart `W'` of `V` over
`W ×_Y V`: the inverse image of `t` along the square `(W', W)`. -/
def IntegralClosedSubspace.baseChangeChartSection (t : L.val.obj (op W))
    (W' : SmallEtale B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor) (k : W' ⟶ V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) :
    ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj
      L).val.obj (op W') :=
  modulePullbackChartSection B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)
    L (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) t

/-- **A free generator of `ℒ` over the charts above `W` restricts to a free generator of `ℒ|_V`
over every chart over `W ×_Y V`.** Freeness is local, so the inverse image of a free generator
generates freely on a covering sieve, and free generation descends along covering sieves. -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.bijective_smul_baseChangeChartSection
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩).property L)
    (e : (W' : SmallEtale B S hS Y) → (W' ⟶ W) → L.val.obj (op W'))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W₁ W₂ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W) (g : W₂ ⟶ W₁),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W₁ k) = e W₂ (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W₁ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS Y hY W₁ ↦ r • e W₁ k)
    (W₁ : SmallEtale B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor) (k : W₁ ⟶ V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) :
    Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor V.isClosedSubspace.1 W₁ ↦
      r • V.baseChangeChartSection hY L W (e W (𝟙 W)) W₁ k := by
  obtain ⟨T, hT, hloc⟩ := exists_sieve_bijective_smul_modulePullbackChartSection B S hS
    (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L hL
    (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) e hcompat hfree
  refine bijective_smul_of_sieve B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
    ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj L)
    W₁ _ T hT fun W₂ ι hι => ?_
  have hEq : (chartRestrictLinear ((modulePullback B S hS
        (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj L) ι)
      (V.baseChangeChartSection hY L W (e W (𝟙 W)) W₁ k) =
      modulePullbackChartSectionRestrict B S hS
        (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L
        (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) (e W (𝟙 W)) (𝟙 W₂ ≫ ι) := by
    unfold modulePullbackChartSectionRestrict
    simp only
    rw [modulePullbackChartFMap_app]
    rfl
  rw [hEq]
  exact hloc ι hι W₂ (𝟙 W₂)

/-- **The restriction of a section `s` to `V`, over a chart `W'` over `W ×_Y V`, is the pullback of
the coordinate of `s` times the restricted generator.** -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.modulePullbackSections_eval_baseChangeChart (s : L.sections)
    (t : L.val.obj (op W)) (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing B S hS Y hY W) (L.val.obj (op W)))
    (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • t = x) (W' : SmallEtale B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor)
    (k : W' ⟶ V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) :
    (modulePullbackSections B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)
        L s).eval (op (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k).U) =
      chartDiagramRestrict B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)
          (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) •
        modulePullbackChartSection B S hS
          (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L
          (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) t := by
  refine (modulePullbackSections_val B S hS
    (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s
    (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k)).trans ?_
  have hs : s.val (op (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k).V) =
      l₀ (s.eval (op W)) • t := (hb _).symm
  rw [hs]
  exact modulePullbackChartSection_smul B S hS
    (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L
    (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) t

/-- **On an affine chart over `W ×_Y V`, the zero scheme of the restriction of `s` to `V` is cut
out by the pullback of the coordinate of `s`.** -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_modulePullbackSections
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩).property L)
    (s : L.sections) (t : L.val.obj (op W))
    (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing B S hS Y hY W) (L.val.obj (op W))) (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • t = x)
    (W' : SmallEtale B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor) (k : W' ⟶ V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)
    (hW' : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toSchemes B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).obj W').1)
    (t' : ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj
      L).val.obj (op W'))
    (ht' : t' = modulePullbackChartSection B S hS
          (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L
          (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) t)
    (l₀' : Module.Dual ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS
      V.subspace.toFunctor V.isClosedSubspace.1).O).obj.obj (op W'))
      (((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj
        L).val.obj (op W')))
    (hb' : ∀ x, l₀' x • t' = x)
    (hinj : ∀ r r' : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS
      V.subspace.toFunctor V.isClosedSubspace.1).O).obj.obj (op W'), r • t' = r' • t' → r = r') :
    definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
        (zeroScheme B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
          ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj
            L)
          (modulePullbackSections B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s)) (op W') =
      Ideal.span
        {chartDiagramRestrict B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)
            (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W k) (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} := by
  rw [definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_eq_span_generator_of_isInvertible B S hS
    ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
    ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj L)
    (isInvertible_modulePullback_obj B S hS
      (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L hL)
    (modulePullbackSections B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s)
    W' hW' t' l₀' hb']
  congr 1
  rw [Set.singleton_eq_singleton_iff]
  have heval := V.modulePullbackSections_eval_baseChangeChart hY L W s t l₀ hb W' k
  rw [← ht'] at heval
  refine hinj _ _ ?_
  rw [hb']
  exact heval

/-- **On the chart `W ×_Y V` of an integral closed subspace, the zero scheme of the restriction of
`s` is cut out by the pullback of the coordinate of `s`**, for a free generator family `e` of `ℒ`
above `W` with coordinate `l₀` at `W`. -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_modulePullbackSections_baseChangeChart
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩).property L)
    (s : L.sections)
    (e : (W' : SmallEtale B S hS Y) → (W' ⟶ W) → L.val.obj (op W'))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W₁ W₂ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W) (g : W₂ ⟶ W₁),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W₁ k) = e W₂ (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W₁ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS Y hY W₁ ↦ r • e W₁ k)
    (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing B S hS Y hY W) (L.val.obj (op W)))
    (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • e W (𝟙 W) = x)
    (hW' : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toSchemes B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).obj
      (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).1) :
    definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
        (zeroScheme B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
          ((modulePullback B S hS (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj
            L)
          (modulePullbackSections B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s))
        (op (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)) =
      Ideal.span
        {chartDiagramRestrict B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)
            (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W (𝟙 (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)))
            (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} := by
  have hbij := V.bijective_smul_baseChangeChartSection hY L W hL e hcompat hfree
    (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) (𝟙 _)
  let e' := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton _ _
    (V.baseChangeChartSection hY L W (e W (𝟙 W)) (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) (𝟙 _))) hbij
  exact V.definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_modulePullbackSections hY L W hL s (e W (𝟙 W)) l₀ hb
    (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) (𝟙 _) hW'
    (V.baseChangeChartSection hY L W (e W (𝟙 W)) (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W) (𝟙 _))
    rfl e'.symm.toLinearMap (fun x => e'.apply_symm_apply x) (fun r r' h => hbij.1 h)

/-- The scheme morphism of the square `(W ×_Y V, W)` at the identity is the projection
`W ×_Y V → W`. -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.toScheme_map_baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram_id :
    (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
        (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W (𝟙 (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))).g =
      V.baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W := by
  change (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS V.subspace.toFunctor).map (𝟙 _) ≫
        (V.baseChangeChartDiagram B S hS hY W).g) = _
  rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, Category.id_comp]

/-- **The colength, at a point `y` of `W ×_Y V`, of the zero scheme of the restriction of `s` to
`V` is the colength in the local ring of `W` at the image of `y` of the coordinate of `s`
together with the ideal of `V`.** -/
theorem IntegralClosedSubspace.length_quotient_definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_baseChangeChart
    (hL : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible (structureCommRings B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS ⟨Y, hY⟩).property L)
    (s : L.sections)
    (e : (W' : SmallEtale B S hS Y) → (W' ⟶ W) → L.val.obj (op W'))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W₁ W₂ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W) (g : W₂ ⟶ W₁),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W₁ k) = e W₂ (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W₁ : SmallEtale B S hS Y) (k : W₁ ⟶ W),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing B S hS Y hY W₁ ↦ r • e W₁ k)
    (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing B S hS Y hY W) (L.val.obj (op W)))
    (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • e W (𝟙 W) = x) [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    [IsAffine (chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))]
    (y : chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)) :
    Module.length ((chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).presheaf.stalk y)
        ((chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).presheaf.stalk y ⧸
          Ideal.map ((chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom
            (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
              (zeroScheme B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
                ((modulePullback B S hS
                  (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj L)
                (modulePullbackSections B S hS
                  (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s))
              (op (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)))) =
      Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk (V.baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W y))
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk (V.baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W y) ⧸
          (Ideal.span {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ (V.baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W y)
            trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} ⊔
            RingHom.ker ((V.baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W).stalkMap y).hom)) := by
  have hdef := V.definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_modulePullbackSections_baseChangeChart hY L W hL s e
    hcompat hfree l₀ hb ‹_›
  have hmap :
      Ideal.map ((chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom
      (definingIdealAt B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
        (zeroScheme B S hS ⟨V.subspace.toFunctor, V.isClosedSubspace.1⟩
          ((modulePullback B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace)).obj L)
          (modulePullbackSections B S hS
            (closedSubspaceHom B S hS hY V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace) L s))
        (op (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))) =
      Ideal.span
        {((chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W)).presheaf.germ ⊤ y trivial).hom
          (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
            (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W
              (𝟙 (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))).g).appTop.hom
              (l₀ (s.eval (op W))))} := by
    rw [hdef]
    exact (Ideal.map_span _ _).trans (congrArg _ Set.image_singleton)
  rw [hmap]
  have : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
      (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W (𝟙 (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))).g) := by
    rw [V.toScheme_map_baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram_id hY W]
    exact V.isClosedImmersion_baseChangeChartProj B S hS hY W
  refine (length_quotient_span_germ_appTop ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
    (V.baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram hY W (𝟙 (V.baseChangeChart B S hS hY W))).g)
    (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) y).trans ?_
  rw [V.toScheme_map_baseChangeChartGeneratorDiagram_id hY W]

end RestrictedSection

/-! ### The branches through a point of a chart -/

section Branches

variable {k : ℤ}
    (hdim : deltaDimensionClosed D sX hX Set.univ isClosed_univ ≤ ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    (W : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (w : chartScheme W)
    (hξ : D.deltaValue sX (chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w) = k)
    (hA : ringKrullDim ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) = 1)

/-- The point of `|X|` under the point of the chart `W` corresponding to a prime of `𝒪_{W, w}`. -/
abbrev chartBranchPoint (q : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    points D.site D.base D.base_mem X :=
  chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q)

/-- The point under the maximal ideal is the point under `w`. -/
theorem chartBranchPoint_closedPoint :
    chartBranchPoint D W w (IsLocalRing.closedPoint _) =
      chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w := by
  rw [chartBranchPoint, Scheme.fromSpecStalk_closedPoint]

/-- The point under a prime of `𝒪_{W, w}` is a generization of the point under `w`. -/
theorem chartBranchPoint_specializes (q : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    chartBranchPoint D W w q ⤳ chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w :=
  (Stacks.Chow.specializes_fromSpecStalk w q).map
    (continuous_chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem W)

include hX hA in
/-- **A minimal prime of `𝒪_{W, w}` does not lie over the point under `w`**, the local ring
having dimension one: both points would have the coheight of the closure of their common image,
which for the minimal prime is zero. -/
theorem chartBranchPoint_ne_of_mem_minimalPrimes
    (q : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w))
    (hq : q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    chartBranchPoint D W w q ≠ chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w := by
  intro h
  have h0 : Order.coheight ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q) = 0 :=
    (Stacks.Chow.coheight_fromSpecStalk_eq_height w q).trans (Ideal.height_eq_zero_iff.mpr hq)
  have hc1 := coheight_eq_codimension_chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
    (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) W ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q)
  have hc2 := coheight_eq_codimension_chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
    (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) W w
  rw [show chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q) =
    chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w from h, ← hc2, h0] at hc1
  have := ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight w
  rw [← hc1, hA] at this
  exact absurd this (by simp)

include hdim hξ hA in
/-- **A minimal prime of `𝒪_{W, w}` lies over a point of δ-dimension `k + 1`**: a strict
generization of a point of δ-dimension `k`, on a space of δ-dimension at most `k + 1`. -/
theorem deltaValue_chartBranchPoint_of_mem_minimalPrimes
    (q : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w))
    (hq : q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    D.deltaValue sX (chartBranchPoint D W w q) = k + 1 := by
  have hlt := (deltaDimensionFunction D sX hX).strictAnti_specializes
    (chartBranchPoint_specializes D W w q)
    (chartBranchPoint_ne_of_mem_minimalPrimes D sX hX W w hA q hq)
  rw [deltaDimensionFunction_apply, deltaDimensionFunction_apply, hξ] at hlt
  have hle := deltaValue_le_of_deltaDimensionClosed_le D sX hX hdim (chartBranchPoint D W w q)
  omega

include hdim in
/-- **A point of maximal δ-value is the generic point of an irreducible component of `|X|`**: any
strict generization would have a larger δ-value. -/
theorem closure_singleton_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_deltaValue_eq
    (x : points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (hx : D.deltaValue sX x = k + 1) :
    closure ({x} : Set (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X)) ∈
      irreducibleComponents (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) := by
  have : QuasiSober (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) := quasiSober_points_of_isGood D sX hX
  refine ⟨isIrreducible_singleton.closure, fun t ht hsub => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := QuasiSober.sober ht.closure isClosed_closure
  have hcx : c ⤳ x := hc.specializes (subset_closure (hsub (subset_closure rfl)))
  have hceq : c = x := by
    by_contra hne
    have hlt := (deltaDimensionFunction D sX hX).strictAnti_specializes hcx (Ne.symm hne ∘ Eq.symm)
    rw [deltaDimensionFunction_apply, deltaDimensionFunction_apply, hx] at hlt
    have hle := deltaValue_le_of_deltaDimensionClosed_le D sX hX hdim c
    omega
  subst hceq
  exact subset_closure.trans (hc.symm ▸ subset_rfl)

include hdim hξ hA in
/-- The integral closed subspace whose generic point is the point under a minimal prime of
`𝒪_{W, w}`: an irreducible component of `X` of δ-dimension `k + 1`. -/
def chartBranchComponent (q : minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    ComponentsOfDeltaDimension D sX hX (k + 1) :=
  ⟨integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX)
      (closureSingleton (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩)),
    ⟨(integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
        (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) _).isClosedSubspace,
      (integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
        (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) _).isIntegralSpace, by
      change subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X _ ∈ _
      rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints]
      exact closure_singleton_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_deltaValue_eq D sX hX hdim _
        (deltaValue_chartBranchPoint_of_mem_minimalPrimes D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA _ q.2)⟩, by
    have : T0Space (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) :=
      t0Space_points_of_isDecentSpace D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
        (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX)
    have hgen := (integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX)
      (closureSingleton (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩))).isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint
        D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
    rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints] at hgen
    have heq := hgen.eq (show IsGenericPoint (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩)
      (closureSingleton (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩) : Set _) from rfl)
    change D.deltaValue sX (IntegralClosedSubspace.ambientGenericPoint _ _ _ _) = _
    rw [heq]
    exact deltaValue_chartBranchPoint_of_mem_minimalPrimes D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA _ q.2⟩

/-- The generic point of `chartBranchComponent` is the point under the minimal prime. -/
theorem ambientGenericPoint_chartBranchComponent
    (q : minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    (chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q).1.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base
        D.base_mem = chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩ := by
  have : T0Space (points D.site D.base D.base_mem X) :=
    t0Space_points_of_isDecentSpace D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX)
  have hgen := (chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q).1.isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint
    D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
  change IsGenericPoint _ (subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X
    (integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX)
      (closureSingleton (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩))).subspace) at hgen
  rw [subspacePointSet_integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints] at hgen
  exact hgen.eq (show IsGenericPoint (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩)
    (closureSingleton (chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩) : Set _) from rfl)

/-- A minimal prime has the component `V` exactly when it lies over the generic point of `V`. -/
theorem chartBranchComponent_eq_iff (q : minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w))
    (V : ComponentsOfDeltaDimension D sX hX (k + 1)) :
    chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q = V ↔
      chartBranchPoint D W w ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩ = V.1.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem := by
  constructor
  · rintro rfl
    exact (ambientGenericPoint_chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q).symm
  · intro h
    refine Subtype.ext (eq_integralClosedSubspaceOfPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX) V.1 _ ?_).symm
    rw [h]
    exact (V.1.isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1).symm

include hξ hA in
/-- **A prime of `𝒪_{W, w}` over the generic point of a component of δ-dimension `k + 1` is a
minimal prime**: it is not the maximal ideal, whose point lies over a point of δ-dimension `k`,
and the local ring has dimension one. -/
theorem mem_minimalPrimes_of_chartBranchPoint_eq
    (V : ComponentsOfDeltaDimension D sX hX (k + 1))
    (q : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w))
    (hq : chartBranchPoint D W w q = V.1.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem) :
    q.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) := by
  refine Ideal.mem_minimalPrimes_of_ne_maximalIdeal hA.le fun hm => ?_
  have hq' : q = IsLocalRing.closedPoint _ := PrimeSpectrum.ext hm
  rw [hq', chartBranchPoint_closedPoint] at hq
  have h1 : D.deltaValue sX (V.1.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem) = k + 1 := V.2.2
  rw [← hq, hξ] at h1
  omega

/-- The ideal of an integral closed subspace `V` in the local ring `𝒪_{W, w}` of an affine chart:
the ideal generated by the defining ideal of `V` over `W`. -/
abbrev chartComponentIdeal [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    (V : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X) :
    Ideal ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) :=
  Ideal.map ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom
    (definingIdealAt D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩ ⟨V.subspace, V.isClosedSubspace⟩ (op W))

/-- At a point of `W ×_X V`, the ideal of `V` in the local ring of `W` is the kernel of the stalk
map of the closed immersion `W ×_X V → W`. -/
theorem chartComponentIdeal_baseChangeChartProj [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    (V : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (y : chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W)) :
    chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W (V.baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W y) V =
      RingHom.ker ((V.baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W).stalkMap y).hom := by
  have := V.isClosedImmersion_baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W
  rw [← stalk_ker_eq_of_affine_target (V.baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W) y ⊤
    (isAffineOpen_top _) trivial]
  exact (stalk_ker_snd_eq_map_germ_definingIdealAt hX.1 V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace W _).symm

/-- **The ideal of an integral closed subspace in a local ring of an affine chart is radical**: at
a point of `W ×_X V` it is the kernel of the stalk map of a reduced closed subscheme, and away
from `V` it is the unit ideal. -/
theorem isRadical_chartComponentIdeal [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    (V : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X) :
    (chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V).IsRadical := by
  by_cases hwV : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w ∈
      subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X V.subspace
  · obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := V.exists_baseChangeChartProj_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W w hwV
    rw [chartComponentIdeal_baseChangeChartProj]
    exact V.isRadical_ker_stalkMap_baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W y
  · unfold chartComponentIdeal
    rw [map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top hX.1 V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace W w hwV]
    exact fun _ _ => trivial

include hdim hξ hA in
/-- **The minimal primes of the ideal of a component `V` of δ-dimension `k + 1` are the minimal
primes of `𝒪_{W, w}` whose branch is `V`.** -/
theorem minimalPrimes_chartComponentIdeal [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    (V : ComponentsOfDeltaDimension D sX hX (k + 1)) :
    (chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V.1).minimalPrimes =
      {q | ∃ h : q ∈ minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w),
        chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA ⟨q, h⟩ = V} := by
  by_cases hwV : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w ∈
      subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X V.1.subspace
  · obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := V.1.exists_baseChangeChartProj_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W w hwV
    subst hy
    rw [chartComponentIdeal_baseChangeChartProj,
      V.1.minimalPrimes_ker_stalkMap_baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W y]
    ext q
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨hq, hqV⟩
      have hmin := mem_minimalPrimes_of_chartBranchPoint_eq D sX hX W _ hξ hA V ⟨q, hq⟩ hqV
      exact ⟨hmin, (chartBranchComponent_eq_iff D sX hX hdim W _ hξ hA ⟨q, hmin⟩ V).mpr hqV⟩
    · rintro ⟨hmin, hc⟩
      exact ⟨hmin.1.1, (chartBranchComponent_eq_iff D sX hX hdim W _ hξ hA ⟨q, hmin⟩ V).mp hc⟩
  · unfold chartComponentIdeal
    rw [map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top hX.1 V.1.subspace V.1.isClosedSubspace W w hwV,
      Ideal.minimalPrimes_top]
    ext q
    refine ⟨fun h => h.elim, fun ⟨hmin, hc⟩ => ?_⟩
    exfalso
    have hpt := (chartBranchComponent_eq_iff D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA ⟨q, hmin⟩ V).mp hc
    refine hwV ?_
    have hspec := chartBranchPoint_specializes D W w ⟨q, hmin.1.1⟩
    rw [hpt] at hspec
    exact hspec.mem_closed (isClosed_subspacePointSet_of_isClosedSubspace D hX.1 V.1.subspace
      V.1.isClosedSubspace)
      (V.1.isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1).mem

/-- **The length of `𝒪_{W, w}` localized at a minimal prime is the multiplicity in `[X]_{k+1}` of
the component that prime lies over**: that localization is the local ring of the chart at the
point of the prime, whose length is the length of `𝒪_X` at its image (Stacks 0EE1). -/
theorem length_localization_eq_fundamentalCycleCoeff_chartBranchComponent
    (γ : points D.site D.base D.base_mem X → GeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (hγ : ∀ x, (γ x).LiesOver x) (q : minimalPrimes ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)) :
    haveI := q.2.1.1
    ((Module.length (Localization.AtPrime q.1) (Localization.AtPrime q.1)).toNat : ℤ) =
      fundamentalCycleCoeff D sX hX (k + 1) γ
        (chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q).1 := by
  have := q.2.1.1
  rw [fundamentalCycleCoeff, cycleCoeffOfModule,
    ite_eq_left (chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA q).2.2,
    ambientGenericPoint_chartBranchComponent]
  set q' : PrimeSpectrum ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) := ⟨q.1, q.2.1.1⟩
  rw [geometricLength_unit_eq_length_stalk ⟨X, hX.1⟩ (γ (chartBranchPoint D W w q')) W
    ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q') (hγ _).symm]
  have hsp := Stacks.Chow.specializes_fromSpecStalk w q'
  let : Algebra ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
      ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q')) :=
    ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalkSpecializes hsp).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsLocalization.AtPrime
      ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q')) q'.asIdeal :=
    Stacks.Chow.isLocalization_stalk_of_specializes hsp q' rfl
  exact congrArg (fun m : ℕ∞ => (m.toNat : ℤ)) (Ideal.length_self_eq_of_ringEquiv
    (IsLocalization.algEquiv q'.asIdeal.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal)
      ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk ((chartScheme W).fromSpecStalk w q'))).toRingEquiv)

end Branches

/-! ### The coefficient of a component zero cycle, read on a chart -/

section ComponentCoefficient

variable (L : Modules.{u, u} D.site D.base D.base_mem X hX.1) (hL : IsInvertibleSheaf D sX hX L)
    (s : L.sections) (k : ℤ) (W : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X) [IsAffine (chartScheme W)]
    (e : (W' : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X) → (W' ⟶ W) → L.val.obj (op W'))
    (hcompat : ∀ (W₁ W₂ : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (k : W₁ ⟶ W) (g : W₂ ⟶ W₁),
      (L.val.map g.op).hom (e W₁ k) = e W₂ (g ≫ k))
    (hfree : ∀ (W₁ : SmallEtale D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (k : W₁ ⟶ W),
      Function.Bijective fun r : chartRing D.site D.base D.base_mem X hX.1 W₁ ↦ r • e W₁ k)
    (l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing D.site D.base D.base_mem X hX.1 W) (L.val.obj (op W)))
    (hb : ∀ x, l₀ x • e W (𝟙 W) = x)

include hL hcompat hfree hb in
/-- **The coefficient of `[Z(s|_V)]_k`, pushed forward to `X`, at an integral closed subspace `T`
of δ-dimension `k`, is the colength of `(f) + I_V` in the local ring `A` of an affine chart at a
point over the generic point of `T`**, `f` being the germ of the coordinate of `s` and `I_V` the
ideal of `V` in `A`. -/
theorem componentZeroCycleCoeff_eq_length_quotient (w : chartScheme W)
    (V : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (γ : points D.site D.base D.base_mem (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).1.toFunctor →
      GeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).1.toFunctor)
    (hγ : ∀ x, (γ x).LiesOver x)
    (T : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (hT : deltaDimension D sX T = k)
    (hw : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w =
      T.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem) :
    componentZeroCycleCoeff D sX hX L s k V γ T =
      ((Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w ⧸
          (Ideal.span {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} ⊔
            chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V))).toNat : ℤ) := by
  have hXdec := isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX
  by_cases hTV : subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X T.subspace ⊆
      subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X V.subspace
  · obtain ⟨TV, rfl⟩ := IntegralClosedSubspace.exists_pushforward_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      V.isClosedSubspace.1 hXdec (isDecentSpace_of_isClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem hXdec
        V.isClosedSubspace) V.isClosedSubspace.2 T hTV
    have hwV : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w ∈
        subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X V.subspace :=
      hTV (hw ▸ (IntegralClosedSubspace.isGenericPoint_ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base
        D.base_mem hX.1 _).mem)
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := V.exists_baseChangeChartProj_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W w hwV
    have := V.isClosedImmersion_baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W
    have : IsAffine (chartScheme (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W)) :=
      isAffine_of_isAffineHom (V.baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W)
    rw [chartComponentIdeal_baseChangeChartProj]
    have hchain := V.length_quotient_definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_baseChangeChart hX.1 L W hL s e
      hcompat hfree l₀ hb y
    rw [← hchain]
    unfold componentZeroCycleCoeff
    rw [cycleClosedPushforward_apply_pushforward]
    -- the point of the chart of `V` under `y` is the generic point of `TV`
    have hyV : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem V.subspace.toFunctor
        (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W) y =
        TV.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem := by
      refine (V.isClosedEmbedding_pointsMap D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1).injective ?_
      rw [← V.chartSchemeToPoints_baseChangeChartProj D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W y, hw,
        IntegralClosedSubspace.ambientGenericPoint_pushforward]
    have hVdec := isDecentSpace_of_isClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem hXdec
      V.isClosedSubspace
    have hδV : deltaDimension D (V.subspace.ι ≫ sX) TV = k := by
      rw [← deltaDimension_closedSubspaceComponentImage D sX hX V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace TV]
      exact hT
    by_cases hTZ : subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem V.subspace.toFunctor TV.subspace ⊆
        subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem V.subspace.toFunctor
          (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).1
    · obtain ⟨T'', rfl⟩ := IntegralClosedSubspace.exists_pushforward_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem
        V.isClosedSubspace.1 (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).2.1 hVdec
        (isDecentSpace_of_isClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem hVdec
          (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).2)
        (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).2.2 TV hTZ
      rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_closedSubspaceComponentImage, ite_eq_left hδV]
      have ha : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem V.subspace.toFunctor
          (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W) y =
          pointsMap D.site D.base D.base_mem (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).1.toFunctor
            (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).1.ι
            (γ (T''.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem)).image := by
        rw [hγ, hyV, IntegralClosedSubspace.ambientGenericPoint_pushforward]
      rw [geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints'
        V.isClosedSubspace.1 (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V)
        (γ (T''.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem))
        (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W) y ha]
    · rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_eq_zero D (V.subspace.ι ≫ sX)
        (isGood_integralClosedSubspace D sX hX V) _ _ k γ TV fun T'' h => hTZ (by
          rw [← h, IntegralClosedSubspace.subspacePointSet_pushforward]
          exact Set.image_subset_range _ _)]
      have hnot := notMem_subspacePointSet_of_ambientGenericPoint_eq D V.isClosedSubspace.1 TV _
        (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V).2 hTZ hyV
      rw [map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top' V.isClosedSubspace.1
        (V.baseChangeChart D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1 W)
        (componentVanishingLocus D sX hX L s V) y hnot]
      rw [Ideal.length_quotient_top_eq_zero]
      rfl
  · unfold componentZeroCycleCoeff
    rw [cycleClosedPushforward_apply_of_forall_ne D hX.1 V.isClosedSubspace.1 hXdec
      V.isClosedSubspace.2 _ T fun T' h => hTV (by
        rw [← h, IntegralClosedSubspace.subspacePointSet_pushforward]
        exact Set.image_subset_range _ _)]
    have hnot := notMem_subspacePointSet_of_ambientGenericPoint_eq D hX.1 T _ V.isClosedSubspace
      hTV hw
    unfold chartComponentIdeal
    rw [map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top hX.1 V.subspace V.isClosedSubspace W w hnot, sup_top_eq]
    rw [Ideal.length_quotient_top_eq_zero]
    rfl

include hL hb in
/-- **The coefficient of `[Z(s)]_k` at an integral closed subspace `T` of δ-dimension `k` is the
colength of `(f)` in the local ring `A` of an affine chart at a point over the generic point of
`T`**, `f` being the germ of the coordinate of `s`. -/
theorem cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_length_quotient (w : chartScheme W)
    (γ : points D.site D.base D.base_mem (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.toFunctor →
      GeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.toFunctor)
    (hγ : ∀ x, (γ x).LiesOver x)
    (T : IntegralClosedSubspace D.site D.base D.base_mem X) (hT : deltaDimension D sX T = k)
    (hw : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w =
      T.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem) :
    cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace D sX hX (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1
        (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2 k γ T =
      ((Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w ⧸
          Ideal.span
            {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom
                (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))})).toNat : ℤ) := by
  have hXdec := isDecentSpace_of_isGood D sX hX
  have hmap := map_germ_definingIdealAt_zeroScheme_eq_span hX.1 W L hL s (e W (𝟙 W)) l₀ hb w
  by_cases hTZ : subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X T.subspace ⊆
      subspacePointSet D.site D.base D.base_mem X (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1
  · obtain ⟨T', rfl⟩ := IntegralClosedSubspace.exists_pushforward_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem hX.1
      (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2.1 hXdec (isDecentSpace_of_isClosedSubspace D.site D.base
        D.base_mem hXdec (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2) (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2.2 T hTZ
    rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_closedSubspaceComponentImage, ite_eq_left hT]
    have ha : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w =
        pointsMap D.site D.base D.base_mem (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.toFunctor
          (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.ι
          (γ (T'.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem)).image := by
      rw [hγ, hw, IntegralClosedSubspace.ambientGenericPoint_pushforward]
    rw [geometricLength_unit_eq_length_quotient_definingIdealAt_of_chartSchemeToPoints'
      hX.1 (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s) (γ (T'.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem))
      W w ha]
    exact congrArg (fun I : Ideal ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) =>
      ((Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
        ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w ⧸ I)).toNat : ℤ)) hmap
  · rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_eq_zero D sX hX _ _ k γ T fun T' h => hTZ (by
      rw [← h, IntegralClosedSubspace.subspacePointSet_pushforward]
      exact Set.image_subset_range _ _)]
    have hnot := notMem_subspacePointSet_of_ambientGenericPoint_eq D hX.1 T _
      (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2 hTZ hw
    have htop := map_germ_definingIdealAt_eq_top' hX.1 W (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s) w hnot
    rw [hmap] at htop
    rw [htop]
    rw [Ideal.length_quotient_top_eq_zero]
    rfl

end ComponentCoefficient

/-! ### Stacks 0EQL -/

section ZeroCycleOfRegularSection

variable (L : Modules.{u, u} D.site D.base D.base_mem X hX.1) (s : L.sections) (k : ℤ)

/-- **Stacks 0EQL, for any geometric representatives.** The identity `[Z(s)]_k = ∑ n_i [Z(s_i)]_k`
of coefficient families holds with the multiplicities read at any families of geometric points
lying over the points they represent.

At an integral closed subspace `T` of δ-dimension `k` choose an affine étale chart `W` of `X`
through the generic point `ξ` of `T` on which `ℒ` is free, and write `A = 𝒪_{W, w}` and `f` for the
germ of the coordinate of `s`. Both sides are colengths in `A`: the left side is that of `(f)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_length_quotient`), the
summand of a component `V` on the right is `n_V` times that of `(f) + I_V`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentZeroCycleCoeff_eq_length_quotient`). If `f` is a unit both
vanish. Otherwise `A` is one-dimensional, `f` is a nonzerodivisor of it, the minimal primes of `A`
are partitioned by the components of δ-dimension `k + 1` they lie over, `I_V` is the radical
ideal of the block of `V`, and `n_V` is the length of `A` localized at any prime of that block;
the grouped form of Stacks 02QG,
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_length_quotient_span_eq_finsum_length_quotient_sup`, is the identity. -/
theorem cycleCoeff_vanishingLocus_eq_componentZeroCycleSumCoeff_of_isRegularSection_of_liesOver
    (hL : IsInvertibleSheaf D sX hX L)
    (hs : AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegularSection (structureCommRings D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩).property s)
    (hdim : deltaDimensionClosed D sX hX Set.univ isClosed_univ ≤ ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    (γ : points D.site D.base D.base_mem X → GeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
    (hγ : ∀ x, (γ x).LiesOver x) (γW : ComponentGeometricRepresentatives D sX hX L s k)
    (hγW : ∀ V x, (γW V x).LiesOver x)
    (γZ : points D.site D.base D.base_mem (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.toFunctor →
      GeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1.toFunctor)
    (hγZ : ∀ x, (γZ x).LiesOver x) :
    cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace D sX hX (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1
        (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2 k γZ =
      componentZeroCycleSumCoeff D sX hX L s k γ γW := by
  funext T
  by_cases hT : deltaDimension D sX T = k
  swap
  · rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace, ite_eq_right hT,
      componentZeroCycleSumCoeff_eq_zero_of_deltaDimension_ne D sX hX L s k γ γW hT]
  -- an affine chart through the generic point of `T` on which `ℒ` is free
  obtain ⟨C, x, hx⟩ := exists_chartSchemeToPoints_eq D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩
    (T.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem)
  obtain ⟨W, κ, hWaff, w, e, hcompat, hfree, hwx⟩ := exists_affine_chart_free_of_chart D.site
    D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩ L (Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.ofAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ hL)
    C x
  have := hWaff
  have hw : chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w =
      T.ambientGenericPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem := by
    rw [← chartSchemeToPoints_map D.site D.base D.base_mem X κ w, hwx, hx]
  let eW := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton _ _ (e W (𝟙 W))) (hfree W (𝟙 W))
  let l₀ : Module.Dual (chartRing D.site D.base D.base_mem X hX.1 W) (L.val.obj (op W)) :=
    eW.symm.toLinearMap
  have hb : ∀ y, l₀ y • e W (𝟙 W) = y := fun y => eW.apply_symm_apply y
  have hreg := (isRegularSection_iff_forall_injective_smul D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩ L
    s).1 hs (op W)
  have hinjg := (injective_smul_eval_iff_injective_mul_generator D.site D.base D.base_mem
    ⟨X, hX.1⟩ L s W (e W (𝟙 W)) l₀ hb).1 hreg
  -- the coordinate of `s` is a nonzerodivisor, and so is its germ
  have hg : l₀ (s.eval (op W)) ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(chartScheme W, ⊤) :=
    mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right.mpr fun r hr => hinjg (hr.trans (zero_mul _).symm)
  let : Algebra Γ(chartScheme W, ⊤) ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) :=
    (chartScheme W).presheaf.algebra_section_stalk (U := ⊤) ⟨w, trivial⟩
  have hloc := (isAffineOpen_top (chartScheme W)).isLocalization_stalk ⟨w, trivial⟩
  have hf : ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) :=
    IsLocalization.nonZeroDivisors_le_comap
      ((isAffineOpen_top (chartScheme W)).primeIdealOf ⟨w, trivial⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl
      ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) hg
  have hξ : D.deltaValue sX (chartSchemeToPoints D.site D.base D.base_mem X W w) = k := by
    rw [hw]
    exact hT
  rw [cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_length_quotient D sX hX L hL s k W e l₀ hb w
    γZ hγZ T hT hw, componentZeroCycleSumCoeff]
  have hterm : ∀ V : ComponentsOfDeltaDimension D sX hX (k + 1),
      fundamentalCycleCoeff D sX hX (k + 1) γ V.1 *
        componentZeroCycleCoeff D sX hX L s k V.1 (γW V) T =
      fundamentalCycleCoeff D sX hX (k + 1) γ V.1 *
        ((Module.length ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
          ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w ⧸
            (Ideal.span {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} ⊔
              chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V.1))).toNat : ℤ) := fun V => by
    rw [componentZeroCycleCoeff_eq_length_quotient D sX hX L hL s k W e hcompat hfree l₀ hb w V.1
      (γW V) (hγW V) T hT hw]
  rw [finsum_congr hterm]
  by_cases hfm : ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w)
  · have hA := Ideal.ringKrullDim_eq_one_of_mem_maximalIdeal
      (ringKrullDim_stalk_chartScheme_le_one D sX hX hdim W w hξ) hf hfm
    have : IsNoetherianRing ((chartScheme W).presheaf.stalk w) :=
      isNoetherianRing_stalk_chartScheme_of_isGood D sX hX W w
    refine natCast_length_quotient_span_eq_finsum_length_quotient_sup _
      (fun a b hab => ?_) hfm hA (chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA)
      (fun V => chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V.1)
      (fun V => isRadical_chartComponentIdeal D sX hX W w V.1)
      (fun V => minimalPrimes_chartComponentIdeal D sX hX hdim W w hξ hA V)
      (fun V => fundamentalCycleCoeff D sX hX (k + 1) γ V.1)
      (fun q => length_localization_eq_fundamentalCycleCoeff_chartBranchComponent D sX hX hdim W
        w hξ hA γ hγ q)
    have h1 :
        (a - b) * ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) = 0 := by
      rw [sub_mul]
      have hab' : ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) * a =
          ((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W))) * b := hab
      rw [mul_comm a, mul_comm b, hab', sub_self]
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_right.mp hf _ h1)
  · have hunit := IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal.mp hfm
    have htop : Ideal.span {((chartScheme W).presheaf.germ ⊤ w trivial).hom (l₀ (s.eval (op W)))} =
        ⊤ := Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mpr hunit
    rw [htop, Ideal.length_quotient_top_eq_zero]
    symm
    refine finsum_eq_zero_of_forall_eq_zero fun V => ?_
    rw [top_sup_eq, Ideal.length_quotient_top_eq_zero]
    simp

/-- **Stacks 0EQL.** In Situation 0EDT let `X/B` be good, let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module,
let `s ∈ Γ(X, ℒ)` be a regular section and assume `dim_δ(X) ≤ k + 1`. Write
`[X]_{k+1} = ∑ n_i [X_i]` over the irreducible components `X_i ⊆ X` of δ-dimension `k + 1` and set
`s_i = s|_{X_i}`. Then

`[Z(s)]_k = ∑ n_i [Z(s_i)]_k`

as `k`-cycles on `X`.

Both sides are coefficient families on the integral closed subspaces of `X`: the left side is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace` at the zero scheme of Stacks 0845, the right
side `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.componentZeroCycleSumCoeff`, the multiplicities being read at the
canonical geometric representatives of the points, as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceCycle` (Stacks 0EE1 makes the choice immaterial, by the
`_of_liesOver` variant of this theorem). -/
theorem cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace_vanishingLocus_eq_componentZeroCycleSumCoeff_of_isRegularSection
    (hL : IsInvertibleSheaf D sX hX L)
    (hs : AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegularSection (structureCommRings D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩)
      (structureRingSheaf D.site D.base D.base_mem ⟨X, hX.1⟩).property s)
    (hdim : deltaDimensionClosed D sX hX Set.univ isClosed_univ ≤ ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    cycleCoeffOfClosedSubspace D sX hX (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).1
        (vanishingLocus D sX hX L s).2 k
        (canonicalGeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem _) =
      componentZeroCycleSumCoeff D sX hX L s k
        (canonicalGeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem X)
        (fun _ => canonicalGeometricPoint D.site D.base D.base_mem _) :=
  cycleCoeff_vanishingLocus_eq_componentZeroCycleSumCoeff_of_isRegularSection_of_liesOver
    D sX hX L s k hL hs hdim _ (canonicalGeometricPoint_image D.site D.base D.base_mem X) _
    (fun _ => canonicalGeometricPoint_image D.site D.base D.base_mem _) _
    (canonicalGeometricPoint_image D.site D.base D.base_mem _)

end ZeroCycleOfRegularSection

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

